   Informatics-INFORMATICS-Annual, Poprad, SLOVAKIA, NOV 13-15, 2024},
Abstract = {The aim of this study was to compare the quality of printed samples that
   were printed using additive technology from commercial and recycled PLA
   (polylactic acid) filament that the authors of this study produced
   themselves. Furthermore this scientific work deals with the optimization
   of parameters during the extrusion of filaments based on polymers, which
   are on a commercial basis, where we also used the process of recycling
   and re-extrusion. Subsequently, additive printing and non-destructive
   testing of the samples were started. These tests are intended to
   determine the future application of the given materials and compare the
   resulting parameters of recycled and non-recycled filament used in 3D
   printing of samples. Microscopic analysis with the help of a Metrotome
   1500 and microscope from Carl Zeiss brings us detailed results from the
   composition of materials and possible defects during 3D printing.},
