   Mechanical Engineering, Balatonfured, HUNGARY, MAY 23-26, 2024},
Abstract = {Titanium alloys are considered advanced and high-value materials due to
   their special properties and high production cost. Titanium alloys are
   often used in the aerospace, automotive and medical industries, due to
   their high strength/weight ratio, corrosion resistance, biocompatibility
   and low thermal expansion characteristics. In addition to structural
   efficiency, titanium alloys are characterized by high corrosion
   resistance and do not cause chemical or immunological reactions in the
   human body. The production of titanium is very expensive, so it is
   important to research technologies that require lower costs. One of
   these is the HDH process, which is used for the cheaper production of
   powder from waste material of titanium alloys. This paper presents the
   quality of the powder obtained by recycling a piece of TiAl6Nb7 titanium
   alloy, which can then be used as a raw material for 3D metal printing,
   which is recent and not yet commonly used.},
