Pages = {481-491},
Note = {3rd Construction Management Workshop-CMW, Ravenna, ITALY, NOV 07-08,
   2024},
Abstract = {In recent years, with the European Green Deal and the Action Plan for
   the Circular Economy, Europe has relaunched the goal of pushing the
   construction sector towards a Circular Economy (CE). However, the
   construction sector is yet one of the most impactful. In order to
   activate circular strategies, 3D printing is a significant application
   with a view to creating sustainable materials for the construction
   sector. Starting from these considerations, the paper illustrates the
   experiences developed in two research projects, the MULTIFId project and
   the E-Adaptive project, about experimentation of facade cladding panels
   printed with additive technology. The research describes first the
   problems arising during production phase and their life-cycle impacts;
   then, how the reduction of criticalities and the better use of recycled
   materials can be supported by Artificial Intelligence (AI) softwares.
   With a view to implementing circular production strategies, the aim is
   to promote the use of sustainable building materials produced through 3D
   printing.},
