Pages = {760-776},
Month = {AUG},
Abstract = {Green design and manufacturing process is one of the core of additive
   manufacturing technology, and excellent design and process are not only
   efficient, but also have high processing precision and high resource
   utilization. This work analyzes green design and manufacturing in
   additive manufacturing from four aspects, namely, printing materials,
   structural design, printing device optimization, and manufacturing
   process optimization. Regarding printing materials, it summarizes the
   commonly used categories, recyclability, and environmental impacts of
   different materials. In terms of structural design, the analysis
   highlights the advantages of additive manufacturing products and
   materials for lightweight applications. For printing device
   optimization, several efficient additive manufacturing products,
   materials, and equipment are evaluated based on green design and
   manufacturing principles. The research also investigates manufacturing
   process optimization by assessing the environmental effects of various
   additive manufacturing techniques. These findings provide valuable
   references and insights for promoting the widespread application of
   high-precision, resource-efficient printing technologies.},
