Month = {SEP},
Abstract = {BackgroundThe integration of artificial intelligence (AI) and 3D
   printing is transforming orthopedic practices, enabling personalized
   treatment, enhanced surgical precision, and innovative prosthetic
   development.ObjectiveThis review investigates how AI and 3D printing
   technologies are revolutionizing orthopedic care by improving patient
   outcomes, facilitating advanced clinical practices, and offering novel
   solutions for complex challenges.MethodsThe review synthesizes current
   literature and practical applications of AI and 3D printing in
   orthopedics, focusing on key areas such as joint replacements, spinal
   surgeries, fracture management, and prosthetics design.ResultsAI
   enhances imaging, diagnostics, and treatment planning through
   data-driven decision-making, while 3D printing allows for the creation
   of patient-specific implants, surgical tools, and ventilated plaster
   casts. These innovations collectively reduce risks, accelerate recovery,
   and improve overall patient care. Additionally, sustainable practices
   like using recycled polymers in 3D printing are
   highlighted.ChallengesKey challenges include high costs, limitations in
   biocompatible materials, data privacy concerns, and the lack of
   standardized regulatory frameworks.ConclusionDespite challenges,
   advancements in AI, materials science, and adaptive manufacturing
   processes show a promising future for the integration of these
   technologies in orthopedics. Interdisciplinary collaboration among
   clinicians, engineers, and AI specialists is essential to overcome
   existing barriers and expand their application, ultimately leading to
   precision-based, patient-centered care.},
