@article{ WOS:001456457600001,
Author = {Vijayenthiran, Viveka and Perera, B. A. K. S. and Kavirathna, Anuki
   Sumalya},
Title = {Convergence of 3D printing with circular economy to improve the
   construction sustainability},
Journal = {SMART AND SUSTAINABLE BUILT ENVIRONMENT},
Year = {2025},
Month = {2025 MAR 24},
Abstract = {PurposeThree-dimensional (3D) printing (3DP), which builds objects layer
   by layer, has gained traction in the construction industry for its
   potential to reduce time, cost and waste while boosting productivity.
   The circular economy (CE) model, an alternative to the traditional
   linear economy, focuses on minimising waste and resource use by
   promoting disassembly, material reuse and recycling. By incorporating CE
   strategies, 3DP can manage waste more effectively, enhancing
   construction sustainability. However, there is a dearth of literature on
   this convergence. Hence, this study explores the convergence of 3DP with
   CE to improve sustainability in construction
   projects.Design/methodology/approachThis study employs a qualitative
   research approach with a survey strategy, incorporating an extensive
   literature review to establish a foundation in the research domain. Data
   collection was conducted using the Delphi technique, which involved
   three iterative rounds of semi-structured interviews with experts. The
   empirical data collected from the expert interviews were analysed using
   manual content analysis.FindingsThe findings reveal 12 positive and 6
   negative impacts of 3DP on sustainability, with 10 applicable CE
   strategies. Further, this study explores how to integrate CE strategies
   to manage the identified impacts and their level of influence. Key CE
   strategies such as designing out waste, waste-free production/waste
   management and BIM-based construction management were identified as
   highly influential across the sustainability
   pillars.Originality/valueThis research makes a significant theoretical
   contribution by being one of the few studies integrating 3DP, CE and
   sustainability within the construction sector. It examines the key
   impacts of 3DP on the pillars of sustainability and proposes CE
   strategies to mitigate those impacts. By addressing this convergence,
   the study fills a notable gap in the existing body of literature while
   offering practical insights into minimising construction waste, cost and
   time, thereby promoting the development of a more sustainable and
   circular built environment.},
